1
00:00:46,585 --> 00:00:48,543
Oh, man.

2
00:00:48,543 --> 00:00:52,502
Lieutenant, we gotta hurry.

3
00:00:52,502 --> 00:00:56,293
Nothing I can do right now.
The road is completely blocked.

4
00:00:56,293 --> 00:00:58,502
We really need an office at NOI.

5
00:00:58,502 --> 00:01:02,335
Can't believe we have to
drive there for every meeting.

6
00:01:02,335 --> 00:01:05,961
They say we're part of NOI,
but it's like we're invisible there.

7
00:01:05,961 --> 00:01:07,877
People bump into me every time I'm at NOI.

8
00:01:07,877 --> 00:01:10,002
It's worse than subway stations.

9
00:01:10,002 --> 00:01:13,002
Wait, are we literally invisible to them?

10
00:01:13,002 --> 00:01:16,961
Another thing, why are we even
lumped together with Violent Crimes?

11
00:01:16,961 --> 00:01:20,669
Is it so hard to make a
Traffic Crimes division?

12
00:01:20,669 --> 00:01:22,085
Captain,

13
00:01:22,085 --> 00:01:26,585
you gotta put your foot down and
tell them to split us from Violent Crimes,

14
00:01:26,585 --> 00:01:28,460
and get us our own office too.

15
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,877
Okay.

16
00:01:29,877 --> 00:01:32,502
We've crossed the Rubicon and casted the dice.

17
00:01:32,502 --> 00:01:34,961
[Cross the Rubicon - To cross the point of no return]
I'm putting my foot down.

18
00:01:34,961 --> 00:01:37,961
[Cast the dice - Betting everything on the last line.]
Good.

19
00:01:37,961 --> 00:01:39,919
And where the hell is the nerd?

20
00:01:39,919 --> 00:01:42,126
Lieutenant, did you hear?

21
00:01:42,126 --> 00:01:47,002
Investigator Cha went to the
EOD training as an observer.

22
00:01:47,002 --> 00:01:50,827
[EOD: Explosive Ordinance Disposal]

23
00:01:59,293 --> 00:02:03,002
He went head-to-head
with the Counter Terrorism unit.

24
00:02:03,002 --> 00:02:05,543
The opponent was a robot to boot.

25
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:09,377
It was a robot match, then.
Because Mr. Cha is practically a robot.

26
00:02:09,377 --> 00:02:12,077
Isn't that an overstatement?

27
00:02:31,085 --> 00:02:33,119
Oh my god!

28
00:02:41,794 --> 00:02:43,794
Human versus robot.

29
00:02:43,794 --> 00:02:47,785
And the human is one of us,
the Traffic Crimes division.

30
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:53,919
The sensor power cable is at the edge
of the circuit. This is a fake.

31
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:57,502
The real trigger is the contact
circuit next to the elad switch.

32
00:04:21,710 --> 00:04:23,585
Investigator Cha beat the robot?

33
00:04:23,585 --> 00:04:27,377
Yes! The robot, defeated by
a human who's practically a robot.

34
00:04:27,377 --> 00:04:29,335
That's crazy.

35
00:04:29,335 --> 00:04:31,126
Revenge of mankind!

36
00:04:31,126 --> 00:04:34,752
AI is no match for humans just yet!

37
00:04:34,752 --> 00:04:38,335
Dong Gi, how's that relevant?

38
00:04:38,335 --> 00:04:40,585
Where did you hear that anyway?

39
00:04:40,585 --> 00:04:44,252
Well, I have my sources.

40
00:04:44,252 --> 00:04:46,785
Do you want me to call him?

41
00:04:50,794 --> 00:04:53,161
Hey! Move!

42
00:05:10,252 --> 00:05:11,919
- Are you all right?
- Oh my, I'm fine.

43
00:05:11,919 --> 00:05:13,252
I'm sorry.

44
00:05:18,043 --> 00:05:23,126
You are under arrest for
traffic violation, reckless driving,

45
00:05:23,126 --> 00:05:25,293
and aggravated robbery.

46
00:05:25,293 --> 00:05:30,202
It's you again! Who are you, anyway?

47
00:05:32,335 --> 00:05:33,877
TCI.

48
00:05:33,877 --> 00:05:36,210
TCI?

49
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,285
Is that a chicken joint?

50
00:05:43,293 --> 00:05:48,585
TCI. Traffic Crime Investigation.

51
00:05:53,543 --> 00:05:55,418
[Episode 1]

52
00:05:55,418 --> 00:05:58,418
- Why is he taking so long?
- Should we go in without him?

53
00:05:58,418 --> 00:06:02,452
We are already late.
A few minutes won't make a difference.

54
00:06:03,627 --> 00:06:06,043
- Oh.
- I'm sorry.

55
00:06:06,043 --> 00:06:09,585
- I was held up-
- By what? You met a robber or something?

56
00:06:09,585 --> 00:06:11,752
Just come. We are late.

57
00:06:11,752 --> 00:06:13,493
You are hopeless.

58
00:06:14,752 --> 00:06:17,043
According to the Prosecutors' Office,

59
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:21,126
rejection rate for detention warrants
reached 25%.

60
00:06:21,126 --> 00:06:23,618
Same for arrest warrants.

61
00:06:24,168 --> 00:06:26,418
These are not mere numbers.

62
00:06:26,418 --> 00:06:30,210
They point to declining trust
toward our investigative efforts.

63
00:06:32,293 --> 00:06:35,043
People do not trust the police.

64
00:06:35,877 --> 00:06:38,293
What do you think is the cause?

65
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:44,168
Well, the bottom line is,

66
00:06:44,168 --> 00:06:47,585
we lack specialized investigators.

67
00:06:47,585 --> 00:06:52,252
As seasoned veterans leave the force,

68
00:06:52,252 --> 00:06:55,710
inexperienced newcomers fill the void.

69
00:06:56,335 --> 00:07:00,126
Detectives are complaining
about too much workload.

70
00:07:00,126 --> 00:07:03,835
Distrust toward us does not come
from staff shortage.

71
00:07:03,835 --> 00:07:06,627
It is from the misconception
that we are above than prosecutors.

72
00:07:06,627 --> 00:07:09,710
We have been given greater powers,
while our system remains outdated.

73
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:10,919
It is bound to cause issues.

74
00:07:10,919 --> 00:07:12,710
What do you mean, misconception?

75
00:07:12,710 --> 00:07:15,335
Are you saying it's our fault?

76
00:07:15,335 --> 00:07:17,293
Who are you blaming, exactly?

77
00:07:17,293 --> 00:07:20,210
I'm not blaming anyone.
I'm merely stating the facts.

78
00:07:20,210 --> 00:07:23,460
People do not want the police
to be above prosecutors.

79
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,710
They want a government body to uphold justice.

80
00:07:25,710 --> 00:07:28,168
We need to clarify our identity first.

81
00:07:28,168 --> 00:07:30,585
Are we a policing body,
or an investigative body?

82
00:07:30,585 --> 00:07:34,085
Identity sounds nice and all,

83
00:07:34,085 --> 00:07:37,794
but you're saying we should deliver
indictment-ready investigations

84
00:07:37,794 --> 00:07:41,085
when we don't have enough
manpower or resources?

85
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:44,252
It is no longer about taking responsibilities.

86
00:07:44,252 --> 00:07:46,335
It's more like a punishment.

87
00:07:46,335 --> 00:07:49,794
- I didn't mean-
- Stop.

88
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:53,543
We are not here to point fingers.

89
00:07:53,543 --> 00:07:56,585
We have gathered here

90
00:07:56,585 --> 00:08:00,502
to find ways to win back people's trust.

91
00:08:04,543 --> 00:08:07,293
Opinions, anyone?

92
00:08:10,126 --> 00:08:12,043
It is too close…

93
00:08:12,710 --> 00:08:15,119
Captain Jung, from TCI?

94
00:08:19,168 --> 00:08:21,827
-Nothing.
-Don't worry, feel free to share.

95
00:08:34,126 --> 00:08:38,161
Well, we need a space…

96
00:08:40,835 --> 00:08:42,252
What?

97
00:08:50,752 --> 00:08:52,418
We need a room, so…

98
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:56,702
A room? What are you…

99
00:09:07,252 --> 00:09:10,835
I mean, an open chatroom,

100
00:09:10,835 --> 00:09:14,835
to share opinions.

101
00:09:19,377 --> 00:09:22,543
Okay. We'll consider it.

102
00:09:22,543 --> 00:09:26,293
No further comments?
Then let's call it a day.

103
00:09:47,377 --> 00:09:48,877
Captain Jung?

104
00:09:48,877 --> 00:09:52,794
Chatroom? That's brilliant.

105
00:09:52,794 --> 00:09:55,835
You NOI guys are really something, huh?

106
00:09:55,835 --> 00:09:59,502
How about we open our own chatroom
at Namgang Station, too?

107
00:09:59,502 --> 00:10:02,085
We might as well, sir.

108
00:10:03,043 --> 00:10:07,377
That was brilliant. You look stressed, though.

109
00:10:07,377 --> 00:10:10,752
Maybe you need a spa room
instead of a chatroom.

110
00:10:10,752 --> 00:10:13,377
So that I can use it too.

111
00:10:13,377 --> 00:10:17,035
Bravo. You're the best.
Keep up the good work.

112
00:10:21,669 --> 00:10:23,085
Yes?

113
00:10:30,168 --> 00:10:31,710
You have a request?

114
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:35,085
I think you should return
the TCI team to Namgang.

115
00:10:35,085 --> 00:10:37,210
It's affecting operation efficiency.

116
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:40,210
What's more, it doesn't make sense.

117
00:10:40,210 --> 00:10:41,585
What does traffic investigation
have to do with violent crimes?

118
00:10:41,585 --> 00:10:46,077
Not to mention organizational overlap
and confusion in the chain of command.

119
00:10:47,752 --> 00:10:49,285
Efficiency, you say?

120
00:10:50,543 --> 00:10:54,293
Usually, when people
use efficiency as a reason,

121
00:10:54,293 --> 00:10:55,710
they have something else in mind.

122
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:59,535
I'm only concerned about our operations.

123
00:11:00,210 --> 00:11:03,669
Do you think TCI is affecting efficiency…

124
00:11:03,669 --> 00:11:06,702
because of Lieutenant Min?

125
00:11:08,043 --> 00:11:10,535
No, ma'am. You misunderstood.

126
00:11:12,252 --> 00:11:14,326
Glad to hear.

127
00:11:16,293 --> 00:11:19,168
TCI is not just a traffic unit.

128
00:11:19,168 --> 00:11:23,335
I believe they will prove
essential in NOI operations,

129
00:11:23,335 --> 00:11:25,835
for both Detective Bureau
and Investigation Bureau.

130
00:11:25,835 --> 00:11:30,326
Today, all violent crimes
have elements of traffic crimes.

131
00:11:32,585 --> 00:11:34,126
Don't you think so?

132
00:11:37,252 --> 00:11:38,794
Let's give them some time.

133
00:11:38,794 --> 00:11:43,293
We'll discus the TCI issue
with the new director.

134
00:11:47,252 --> 00:11:50,535
Anything else?

135
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:53,326
No, ma'am.

136
00:12:08,293 --> 00:12:09,460
Just wait and see.

137
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:13,585
Like I said, as part of NOI,
we can pick our own cases.

138
00:12:13,585 --> 00:12:18,210
It means we can dig up
those old unsolved cases.

139
00:12:18,210 --> 00:12:20,126
The illegal taxi case.

140
00:12:20,126 --> 00:12:21,794
We gotta see it through.

141
00:12:36,585 --> 00:12:40,043
Hey, Lieutenant!

142
00:12:40,043 --> 00:12:42,961
I told you not to park like this!

143
00:12:42,961 --> 00:12:46,126
Why? This is how I park!

144
00:12:46,126 --> 00:12:48,043
I'm not riding with you any more.

145
00:13:04,126 --> 00:13:06,085
When he said 'room,'

146
00:13:06,085 --> 00:13:09,085
I didn't think that room
would be in the cyber space.

147
00:13:09,085 --> 00:13:13,335
I was a little excited,
and now I'm ashamed.

148
00:13:13,335 --> 00:13:16,252
Captain, what happened to Rubicon?

149
00:13:16,252 --> 00:13:18,577
You said the dice was casted!

150
00:13:19,126 --> 00:13:20,585
According to Sun Tzu,

151
00:13:20,585 --> 00:13:22,543
one should know what battles to pick.

152
00:13:22,543 --> 00:13:25,293
[Pick your battles]
You need to know when to advance and retreat.

153
00:13:25,293 --> 00:13:27,502
[Know when to advance or retreat]
That's how you save yourself from ruin.

154
00:13:27,502 --> 00:13:30,335
Yeah, Sun Tzu would be so proud of you.

155
00:13:30,335 --> 00:13:31,335
And you know this saying?

156
00:13:31,335 --> 00:13:33,752
-"Keep your word."
-You saw how it was.

157
00:13:33,752 --> 00:13:36,126
If I hadn't thought on my feet,

158
00:13:36,126 --> 00:13:38,543
we'd been buried alive.

159
00:13:38,543 --> 00:13:40,669
We already are.

160
00:13:40,669 --> 00:13:42,460
We don't even have a room at NOI.

161
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:45,252
We work for NOI,
but we are Namgang Station's TCI.

162
00:13:45,252 --> 00:13:47,835
We have to walk that direction,
and the other direction.

163
00:13:47,835 --> 00:13:49,752
It's like we're in the intersection.

164
00:13:49,752 --> 00:13:51,669
No.

165
00:13:51,669 --> 00:13:54,252
We're in the complement, not intersection.

166
00:14:02,335 --> 00:14:03,835
We're not in the intersection.

167
00:14:03,835 --> 00:14:08,418
We're neither in A nor B.
We could be here, or there.

168
00:14:09,835 --> 00:14:11,368
Thus, complement.

169
00:14:12,502 --> 00:14:15,126
Yeah, complement.

170
00:14:15,126 --> 00:14:17,543
Thanks for the clarification.

171
00:14:17,543 --> 00:14:22,377
If I had you as a teacher,
I wouldn't have given up on math.

172
00:14:24,794 --> 00:14:26,418
Superintendent!

173
00:14:26,418 --> 00:14:28,252
- Ma'am.
- How can I help you?

174
00:14:28,252 --> 00:14:29,335
A case.

175
00:14:29,335 --> 00:14:32,835
Chief, we just got back from NOI.

176
00:14:32,835 --> 00:14:34,418
Hey!

177
00:14:34,418 --> 00:14:36,710
You're here to work, right?

178
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:40,502
This is not a hotel, you know.

179
00:14:40,502 --> 00:14:41,794
If you don't want to work, just leave.

180
00:14:41,794 --> 00:14:43,418
Ugh, who said I wasn't going to do it?

181
00:14:43,418 --> 00:14:46,752
Ever since you got pregnant,
you've gotten awfully touchy.

182
00:14:46,752 --> 00:14:48,877
So don't get on my nerves.

183
00:14:48,877 --> 00:14:51,835
The hormones are really acting up.

184
00:14:51,835 --> 00:14:54,377
Well, you did the deed, so-

185
00:14:54,377 --> 00:14:56,502
I did the deed?

186
00:14:56,502 --> 00:14:59,210
He went full beast mode, like…

187
00:15:05,002 --> 00:15:08,502
You make me say the darndest things.

188
00:15:08,502 --> 00:15:12,119
Anyway, hang in there, guys.

189
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:15,702
Take care, ma'am.

190
00:15:16,835 --> 00:15:19,377
Well, she's definitely off the promotion race.

191
00:15:19,377 --> 00:15:20,835
What a shame, she worked so hard.

192
00:15:20,835 --> 00:15:21,961
But the "beast" happened.

193
00:15:21,961 --> 00:15:25,002
- That's why I don't get married.
- Don't, or can't?

194
00:15:25,002 --> 00:15:26,702
Sorry.

195
00:15:31,126 --> 00:15:34,794
[Naeguro 20-gil Automobile-bicycle crash]

196
00:15:34,794 --> 00:15:37,210
Crashed with a bicycle…

197
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:40,335
[Two killed, one injured]

198
00:15:42,502 --> 00:15:45,335
[Driver alleges unintended acceleration]

199
00:16:17,627 --> 00:16:20,168
The driver was 36 years old, Han Soo In.

200
00:16:20,168 --> 00:16:22,919
She was driving her husband to work.

201
00:16:22,919 --> 00:16:24,752
She's in the hospital.

202
00:16:24,752 --> 00:16:28,252
Her husband had passed away
when the rescue team arrived.

203
00:16:28,252 --> 00:16:29,794
What about the passenger seatbelt?

204
00:16:29,794 --> 00:16:34,002
According to the responders,
he wasn't wearing a seatbelt.

205
00:16:34,002 --> 00:16:36,877
The passenger airbag didn't work, either.

206
00:16:36,877 --> 00:16:39,377
The driver airbag worked fine, though.

207
00:16:39,377 --> 00:16:43,794
The driver said something over and over.

208
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:46,168
I didn't do it.

209
00:16:46,168 --> 00:16:48,794
The car moved by itself.

210
00:16:48,794 --> 00:16:51,627
The car went crazy.

211
00:16:51,627 --> 00:16:54,252
She claimed sudden acceleration?

212
00:16:54,252 --> 00:16:55,961
You can say that.

213
00:16:57,335 --> 00:17:01,085
Pedal dash cam… nope.

214
00:17:01,877 --> 00:17:04,585
Hey, what are you doing!

215
00:17:04,585 --> 00:17:06,710
Back up! Leave!

216
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:10,002
Leave the area!

217
00:17:10,002 --> 00:17:11,043
You can't do that.

218
00:17:11,043 --> 00:17:14,377
I said leave.

219
00:17:17,669 --> 00:17:21,168
What's happening? No, no!

220
00:17:21,168 --> 00:17:22,710
Honey!

221
00:17:25,293 --> 00:17:29,002
Recording indicates sudden acceleration.

222
00:17:29,002 --> 00:17:30,794
That's what they all say.

223
00:17:30,794 --> 00:17:34,002
"The car went berserk.
It went out of control."

224
00:17:34,002 --> 00:17:35,794
[EDR: Endpoint Detection and Response]
But EDR shows

225
00:17:35,794 --> 00:17:40,210
[EDR: Endpoint Detection and Response]
they mistook gas for brake in 99% of cases.

226
00:17:40,210 --> 00:17:43,585
Like the Gangnam Station crash.

227
00:17:43,585 --> 00:17:45,919
No sudden acceleration claim
has been accepted in court.

228
00:17:45,919 --> 00:17:48,794
Right? It's so obvious.

229
00:17:48,794 --> 00:17:51,377
This crash claimed two lives,

230
00:17:51,377 --> 00:17:53,126
including her husband.

231
00:17:53,126 --> 00:17:55,335
Whatever the facts are,

232
00:17:55,335 --> 00:17:57,877
the driver is going through hell.

233
00:17:57,877 --> 00:18:01,418
So, let's not jump to conclusions
until we get the forensic results.

234
00:18:01,418 --> 00:18:02,961
Right.

235
00:18:02,961 --> 00:18:07,168
Do they have children?

236
00:18:07,168 --> 00:18:08,210
No.

237
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:11,627
The registration card says
the husband is her only family.

238
00:18:11,627 --> 00:18:14,835
Passenger airbag had been manually disabled.

239
00:18:14,835 --> 00:18:19,043
It should have been enabled,
unless they had a booster seat.

240
00:18:19,043 --> 00:18:22,326
Someone did this on purpose,
expecting an accident?

241
00:18:23,627 --> 00:18:26,535
Now that you mention this,
Dong Gi, run the clip again.

242
00:18:29,043 --> 00:18:31,210
What's happening? No, no!

243
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:33,293
Honey!

244
00:18:36,210 --> 00:18:38,210
The husband was so quiet.

245
00:18:38,210 --> 00:18:40,043
Despite his wife's desperate cries.

246
00:18:40,043 --> 00:18:44,210
You're right. Even if he was asleep,
in such a situation…

247
00:18:44,210 --> 00:18:47,002
The passenger did not wear the seatbelt, right?

248
00:18:47,002 --> 00:18:50,085
Could it be the wife?

249
00:18:50,085 --> 00:18:53,669
If the wife had planned it,
she wouldn't have cried out like this.

250
00:18:53,669 --> 00:18:56,794
She was acting because
she knows they have a dash cam.

251
00:18:56,794 --> 00:18:59,085
Don't get ahead of yourselves.

252
00:18:59,085 --> 00:19:00,502
One step at a time, okay?

253
00:19:00,502 --> 00:19:03,794
Sure, but we have to alert
the insurance association, right?

254
00:19:03,794 --> 00:19:06,410
What's the husband's insurance?

255
00:19:06,919 --> 00:19:08,752
Why? Did I say something wrong?

256
00:19:08,752 --> 00:19:11,919
- Yeon Ho and So Hee, you-
- Check on the driver, got it.

257
00:19:11,919 --> 00:19:13,543
Okay, then.

258
00:19:13,543 --> 00:19:16,627
- Hyun Kyung and Dong Gi,
- We'll take statements.

259
00:19:18,418 --> 00:19:21,252
I'll contact NFS, then.

260
00:19:21,252 --> 00:19:23,377
Let's alert the insurance association first.

261
00:19:23,377 --> 00:19:26,035
Lieutenant told you not to get ahead.

262
00:19:26,752 --> 00:19:29,877
- Hey.
- Sir.

263
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:34,502
Your chief is here,
and you guys start sitting down?

264
00:19:34,502 --> 00:19:37,460
Everything's backwards in here!

265
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:40,126
Anyway, is that true?

266
00:19:40,126 --> 00:19:43,002
- What do you mean…
- I mean, that case!

267
00:19:43,961 --> 00:19:46,794
About the father, is is true?

268
00:19:46,794 --> 00:19:49,126
Whose father, sir?

269
00:19:49,126 --> 00:19:51,794
Is "True" the father's name?

270
00:19:51,794 --> 00:19:53,919
You little…

271
00:19:53,919 --> 00:19:55,919
That's not even funny.

272
00:19:55,919 --> 00:20:00,502
Is the driver's father a judge?

273
00:20:00,502 --> 00:20:01,961
Is it true

274
00:20:01,961 --> 00:20:05,502
that the driver's father is a judge?

275
00:20:05,502 --> 00:20:07,119
- Huh?
- Huh?

276
00:20:07,961 --> 00:20:10,043
What, you didn't know?

277
00:20:10,627 --> 00:20:12,669
This is Lieutenant Min, right?

278
00:20:12,669 --> 00:20:14,502
Judge's daughter claims sudden acceleration.

279
00:20:14,502 --> 00:20:15,627
"Nangam" Station…

280
00:20:15,627 --> 00:20:17,585
Can't believe they botched the spelling.

281
00:20:17,585 --> 00:20:19,210
It's just embarrassing.

282
00:20:19,210 --> 00:20:20,919
Are you okay with taking the case?

283
00:20:20,919 --> 00:20:23,710
I think you should let it go.

284
00:20:23,710 --> 00:20:26,669
We can't. It came to us.

285
00:20:26,669 --> 00:20:28,919
And we've gone metropolitan, you know.

286
00:20:28,919 --> 00:20:30,752
Metropolitan my butt.

287
00:20:30,752 --> 00:20:34,377
You play it wrong, and you'll
get crushed from both sides.

288
00:20:34,377 --> 00:20:36,377
Which side are you gonna pick?

289
00:20:36,377 --> 00:20:37,835
What do you even mean?

290
00:20:37,835 --> 00:20:39,335
We have to uncover the truth-

291
00:20:39,335 --> 00:20:40,835
No, I mean,

292
00:20:40,835 --> 00:20:44,043
whose side is the truth on?

293
00:20:44,043 --> 00:20:46,585
Whether it's sudden acceleration
or the driver's fault,

294
00:20:46,585 --> 00:20:48,377
no matter what it is,

295
00:20:48,377 --> 00:20:51,961
you guys will be in a pickle.

296
00:20:51,961 --> 00:20:54,210
Just think about it.

297
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:58,585
Reporters will ask all sorts of questions,
like whether there was political pressure.

298
00:20:58,585 --> 00:21:02,293
My head hurts just thinking about it.

299
00:21:02,293 --> 00:21:04,961
You are giving us pressure right now.

300
00:21:04,961 --> 00:21:06,585
Just let us do our job.

301
00:21:06,585 --> 00:21:08,377
I'm just worried.

302
00:21:08,377 --> 00:21:11,710
You guys gave me so much stress last year.

303
00:21:11,710 --> 00:21:14,126
Now I've got diabetes, hypertension-

304
00:21:14,126 --> 00:21:16,543
- Drinking gives you diabetes, Hyun Kyung.
- Correct.

305
00:21:16,543 --> 00:21:18,961
Don't you say weird things.

306
00:21:18,961 --> 00:21:22,710
Did you dye your hair?

307
00:21:22,710 --> 00:21:24,961
No, but I'm going to.

308
00:21:24,961 --> 00:21:28,919
So you're considering it?

309
00:21:28,919 --> 00:21:31,835
Yeon Ho, you're wearing glasses again?

310
00:21:32,669 --> 00:21:33,877
I had a haircut.

311
00:21:33,877 --> 00:21:35,502
He lost weight.

312
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:37,085
She got a glowup.

313
00:21:37,085 --> 00:21:39,502
That's just a lie.
You guys heard him right?

314
00:21:39,502 --> 00:21:40,585
Investigate this properly!

315
00:21:40,585 --> 00:21:44,075
- Yes, sir!
- I'm not finished!

316
00:21:44,669 --> 00:21:46,794
I dyed my hair, too!

317
00:21:46,794 --> 00:21:48,961
You didn't notice?
Why is nobody concerned?

318
00:21:48,961 --> 00:21:50,502
I said I dyed my hair, too!

319
00:22:00,252 --> 00:22:02,202
Is he… gone?

320
00:22:05,502 --> 00:22:07,202
Both of them?

321
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,869
Can I help you?

322
00:22:19,543 --> 00:22:21,377
We're the police.

323
00:22:21,377 --> 00:22:25,502
I need to ask Ms. Han
a few things about the accident.

324
00:22:25,502 --> 00:22:28,252
- She is…
- It's okay, Mom.

325
00:22:29,168 --> 00:22:31,126
Can you get me some fruit?

326
00:22:31,126 --> 00:22:33,752
- There's some here…
- I want something else.

327
00:22:45,377 --> 00:22:48,961
Go on, ask your questions.

328
00:22:48,961 --> 00:22:50,252
How are you feeling?

329
00:22:50,252 --> 00:22:51,919
I'm fine.

330
00:22:52,502 --> 00:22:57,168
But my parents insisted
that I stay in the hospital.

331
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:01,043
You mentioned it was sudden acceleration?

332
00:23:01,043 --> 00:23:04,535
Could you please share what happened?

333
00:23:10,961 --> 00:23:13,919
Nothing was out of ordinary that morning.

334
00:23:13,919 --> 00:23:18,585
I usually drive my husband to work.

335
00:23:18,585 --> 00:23:23,126
He had been working late every day.

336
00:23:23,126 --> 00:23:26,377
He fell asleep once he got on
the car that day too.

337
00:23:26,377 --> 00:23:28,710
I just thought he must be tired.

338
00:23:32,043 --> 00:23:33,835
What's happening?

339
00:23:35,961 --> 00:23:39,326
No, no, why?

340
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:42,585
What's happening? No, no!

341
00:23:42,585 --> 00:23:44,502
Honey!

342
00:23:50,585 --> 00:23:53,794
I hit the brake to the floor,
but it didn't work.

343
00:23:54,335 --> 00:23:56,919
The steering wheel was out of control.

344
00:23:58,210 --> 00:24:00,243
When I realised what happened…

345
00:24:01,710 --> 00:24:06,410
Was your husband wearing the seatbelt?

346
00:24:07,168 --> 00:24:09,502
I don't know for sure, but…

347
00:24:09,502 --> 00:24:11,543
he should have been.

348
00:24:11,543 --> 00:24:15,961
Otherwise, the alarm goes off.
But they didn't.

349
00:24:17,043 --> 00:24:19,669
I heard you trying to wake him up.

350
00:24:19,669 --> 00:24:22,669
But according to the dash cam clip,
it seemed like he didn't wake up.

351
00:24:22,669 --> 00:24:25,161
Not even the slightest response.

352
00:24:25,669 --> 00:24:28,627
You're right. He slept through it.

353
00:24:28,627 --> 00:24:32,252
The passenger airbag didn't work.

354
00:24:32,252 --> 00:24:35,002
Did you disable it on purpose?

355
00:24:35,002 --> 00:24:36,168
Disabled?

356
00:24:36,168 --> 00:24:37,835
The airbag.

357
00:24:37,835 --> 00:24:40,952
Records say you don't have children.

358
00:24:42,002 --> 00:24:43,794
You're right.

359
00:24:43,794 --> 00:24:47,252
Except for the one I'm carrying here.

360
00:24:47,252 --> 00:24:49,669
Then why did you disable it?

361
00:24:49,669 --> 00:24:52,543
You need a mechanic to do that.

362
00:24:52,543 --> 00:24:54,502
I didn't even know you could do that.

363
00:24:54,502 --> 00:24:57,627
Your husband doesn't have a license.
If you didn't disable it-

364
00:24:57,627 --> 00:25:00,161
I had no idea.

365
00:25:14,835 --> 00:25:16,710
Officers, I presume?

366
00:25:16,710 --> 00:25:20,161
I am her father.

367
00:25:25,543 --> 00:25:28,585
100% pressure on the gas
right up until collision.

368
00:25:28,585 --> 00:25:31,210
No pressure detected on the brake.

369
00:25:31,210 --> 00:25:34,418
The driver did not use the brake.

370
00:25:34,418 --> 00:25:36,543
All control systems were normal.

371
00:25:36,543 --> 00:25:39,293
[ESC: Electronic Stability Control]
No ESC or SCC error, either.

372
00:25:39,293 --> 00:25:42,043
[SCC: Smart Cruise Control]
What are the chances for sudden acceleration?

373
00:25:42,043 --> 00:25:46,418
My money is on driver error,
not sudden acceleration.

374
00:25:46,418 --> 00:25:48,961
There was no mechanical issue.

375
00:25:48,961 --> 00:25:51,835
However, some CAN data are missing,

376
00:25:51,835 --> 00:25:55,585
[CAN: Controller Area Network]
at around 1.6 seconds before collision.

377
00:25:55,585 --> 00:25:57,168
It means…

378
00:25:57,168 --> 00:26:00,460
The car's system signals
went dead for a second.

379
00:26:00,460 --> 00:26:02,961
Sensor power issue,

380
00:26:02,961 --> 00:26:05,210
electric interference…

381
00:26:05,210 --> 00:26:06,919
Anything could have caused it.

382
00:26:06,919 --> 00:26:08,293
Not a major issue, then?

383
00:26:08,293 --> 00:26:11,293
"Nothing significant to report" for now.

384
00:26:11,293 --> 00:26:13,585
-All right, thank you.
-Thank you.

385
00:26:19,335 --> 00:26:22,502
- This car…
- It came in a few days ago.

386
00:26:22,502 --> 00:26:24,168
A hit-and-run.

387
00:26:25,002 --> 00:26:26,460
With VIN damaged and

388
00:26:26,460 --> 00:26:29,168
the number plate missing,
we can't identify the owner.

389
00:26:29,168 --> 00:26:31,669
We are checking for possible DNA.

390
00:26:31,669 --> 00:26:33,460
Have you had any luck?

391
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:35,043
No.

392
00:26:38,168 --> 00:26:40,543
Still looking, are you?

393
00:26:42,168 --> 00:26:44,335
The driver who killed your wife.

394
00:26:49,543 --> 00:26:51,460
You met the judge?

395
00:26:51,460 --> 00:26:53,418
Yeah, it was so awkward.

396
00:26:53,418 --> 00:26:55,710
What did he say?

397
00:26:55,710 --> 00:26:58,585
"I have total faith
in the forensic report.

398
00:26:58,585 --> 00:27:00,752
- However,
- However,

399
00:27:00,752 --> 00:27:04,126
I didn't raise a senseless child.

400
00:27:04,126 --> 00:27:05,752
- Please leave all possibilities open
- Please leave all possibilities open

401
00:27:05,752 --> 00:27:08,794
until you reach a concrete conclusion."

402
00:27:08,794 --> 00:27:10,502
He's a judge, all right.

403
00:27:10,502 --> 00:27:12,460
And his closing statement,

404
00:27:12,460 --> 00:27:15,835
"I'm a Supreme Court Justice, but
you must not let that affect anything."

405
00:27:15,835 --> 00:27:19,002
Huh? So is he pressuring you or not?

406
00:27:19,002 --> 00:27:20,377
Exactly.

407
00:27:20,377 --> 00:27:23,835
"Don't think about the elephant,"
and you end up thinking about it.

408
00:27:23,835 --> 00:27:26,794
Elephant… that's difficult.

409
00:27:26,794 --> 00:27:28,293
Stop.

410
00:27:29,293 --> 00:27:32,669
I hear the superintendent's voice.

411
00:27:35,002 --> 00:27:37,002
What's going on?

412
00:27:37,002 --> 00:27:40,377
-Are they laughing?
-This is a traffic investigation, right?

413
00:27:40,377 --> 00:27:43,502
This is no place for laughter.

414
00:27:57,252 --> 00:27:59,377
Who is that? A celebrity?

415
00:27:59,377 --> 00:28:01,377
The uniform looks good on him.

416
00:28:01,377 --> 00:28:03,377
Is he an idol?

417
00:28:03,377 --> 00:28:05,377
He must be filming something here.

418
00:28:05,377 --> 00:28:06,919
Let's go.

419
00:28:09,460 --> 00:28:11,168
Ma'am?

420
00:28:14,961 --> 00:28:17,252
He is our new trainee.

421
00:28:17,252 --> 00:28:20,961
It's the first day of the
trainee rotation program.

422
00:28:21,835 --> 00:28:24,877
And we drew the long straw!

423
00:28:24,877 --> 00:28:27,085
You are weirdly happy.
Aren't you pregnant?

424
00:28:27,085 --> 00:28:30,252
Can I not be happy
just because I'm pregnant?

425
00:28:30,252 --> 00:28:32,168
After being stuck with you guys all this time,

426
00:28:32,168 --> 00:28:36,669
he's a sight to the sore eyes.
The baby will love it, too.

427
00:28:36,669 --> 00:28:40,002
I'm so happy for you, little one.

428
00:28:40,002 --> 00:28:42,043
Dae Se, let me introduce you.

429
00:28:42,043 --> 00:28:44,627
They are your seniors from TCI.

430
00:28:44,627 --> 00:28:46,752
Wow, no way!

431
00:28:46,752 --> 00:28:49,293
Traffic Crimes Investigation, right?

432
00:28:49,293 --> 00:28:51,202
I saw the news last year.

433
00:28:52,002 --> 00:28:53,627
Salute!

434
00:28:53,627 --> 00:28:57,085
Central Police Academy, Class 317,
Trainee Ji Dae Se, reporting!

435
00:28:57,085 --> 00:28:58,752
It's an honor to meet you!

436
00:28:58,752 --> 00:29:00,961
Honor, right…

437
00:29:00,961 --> 00:29:02,877
- Hi, I'm Min So Hee.
- Glad to meet you.

438
00:29:02,877 --> 00:29:05,168
- Eo Hyun Kyung.
- How do you do.

439
00:29:05,168 --> 00:29:08,168
Does the Traffic Division
hire people by looks?

440
00:29:08,168 --> 00:29:10,835
Everyone is so good looking.

441
00:29:10,835 --> 00:29:12,710
I mean,

442
00:29:12,710 --> 00:29:14,252
look at our beautiful chief.

443
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,335
What are you even saying?

444
00:29:16,335 --> 00:29:18,919
Come here, you!

445
00:29:18,919 --> 00:29:20,002
Wow!

446
00:29:20,002 --> 00:29:21,952
I'm older than I look.

447
00:29:24,961 --> 00:29:26,669
Excuse us, ma'am.

448
00:29:26,669 --> 00:29:28,377
Stay here for a few days.

449
00:29:28,377 --> 00:29:30,043
There are people watching.

450
00:29:30,043 --> 00:29:32,543
If you go home, it will rile them up.

451
00:29:32,543 --> 00:29:35,961
She needs to be at the funeral.

452
00:29:35,961 --> 00:29:38,418
And let her face the humiliation?

453
00:29:39,794 --> 00:29:43,119
You explain things to the in-laws.

454
00:29:43,877 --> 00:29:46,543
Can't you even drive?

455
00:29:47,585 --> 00:29:49,210
And you had run your mouth.

456
00:29:49,210 --> 00:29:50,418
I meant what I said.

457
00:29:50,418 --> 00:29:51,460
Who would believe you?

458
00:29:51,460 --> 00:29:52,585
I didn't lie!

459
00:29:52,585 --> 00:29:54,877
- I have never-
- Darling.

460
00:29:54,877 --> 00:29:56,618
Please.

461
00:29:59,502 --> 00:30:01,827
What are you worried about?

462
00:30:02,377 --> 00:30:04,827
Me, or your reputation?

463
00:30:05,335 --> 00:30:07,543
Or the company?

464
00:30:07,543 --> 00:30:10,869
Are you worried this will affect the company?

465
00:30:17,293 --> 00:30:20,335
All case records are here.

466
00:30:20,335 --> 00:30:22,961
If you have questions, ask the captain.

467
00:30:22,961 --> 00:30:26,418
- The evidence room is…
- He's so green! I was once like that.

468
00:30:26,418 --> 00:30:28,794
Are you for real? Just look at that photo.

469
00:30:28,794 --> 00:30:32,585
That photo betrayed me!

470
00:30:32,585 --> 00:30:35,335
Inspector Cha, you seen this?
He looks like a high schooler!

471
00:30:35,335 --> 00:30:37,835
- He's hitting me, Captain!
- I didn't!

472
00:30:37,835 --> 00:30:40,710
- I had a late night snack.
- Captain!

473
00:30:40,710 --> 00:30:41,919
- That's why I look so big.
- Whatever.

474
00:30:41,919 --> 00:30:44,085
Dong Gi! Let's start the meeting.

475
00:30:44,085 --> 00:30:46,002
- Sorry, sir.
- Okay.

476
00:30:46,002 --> 00:30:48,418
- The wrinkles…
- Right?

477
00:30:48,418 --> 00:30:51,710
Captain? He wants to sit in our meeting.

478
00:30:51,710 --> 00:30:53,627
I'll just watch.

479
00:30:54,335 --> 00:30:55,627
Take a seat.

480
00:30:55,627 --> 00:30:57,126
Just watch.

481
00:30:57,126 --> 00:30:59,627
Don't listen.

482
00:30:59,627 --> 00:31:01,252
You laughed? Is this a joke to you?

483
00:31:01,252 --> 00:31:03,335
- Sorry, sir.
- Dong Gi.

484
00:31:03,335 --> 00:31:05,043
Come.

485
00:31:07,543 --> 00:31:09,877
How was the meeting with Han Soo In?

486
00:31:09,877 --> 00:31:12,168
She is sticking with sudden acceleration.

487
00:31:12,168 --> 00:31:15,752
Says the husband didn't wake up,
she thinks it's strange too.

488
00:31:15,752 --> 00:31:18,543
-The airbag?
-She said she did not disable it.

489
00:31:18,543 --> 00:31:19,752
Except for the baby in her tummy,

490
00:31:19,752 --> 00:31:21,835
there were no children.

491
00:31:21,835 --> 00:31:25,377
I don't think she was lying when she said
she didn't know how to disable it..

492
00:31:25,377 --> 00:31:30,202
Many drivers don't know much about their cars.

493
00:31:31,168 --> 00:31:34,502
I met her father, the judge.

494
00:31:34,502 --> 00:31:36,585
He told me to ignore his position.

495
00:31:36,585 --> 00:31:38,794
No way! It's that case, right?

496
00:31:38,794 --> 00:31:41,577
The one where the judge's daughter
claims sudden acceleration! Right?

497
00:31:42,418 --> 00:31:45,377
Seriously… who said you could speak?

498
00:31:45,377 --> 00:31:47,085
I said just watch!

499
00:31:47,085 --> 00:31:49,126
I'm sorry.

500
00:31:49,126 --> 00:31:51,502
How about the people close to her?

501
00:31:51,502 --> 00:31:52,627
Before we get to that,

502
00:31:52,627 --> 00:31:55,710
let me show you the insurance records.

503
00:31:55,710 --> 00:31:58,919
Like I expected, there are policies
covering the husband, Baek Sung Min.

504
00:31:58,919 --> 00:32:01,710
Two life insurance, worth 1.2 billion won.

505
00:32:01,710 --> 00:32:03,452
The beneficiary is

506
00:32:04,043 --> 00:32:05,085
Han Soo In of course.

507
00:32:05,085 --> 00:32:07,752
- When did they sign up?
- Around three years ago.

508
00:32:07,752 --> 00:32:08,877
That's quite long ago.

509
00:32:08,877 --> 00:32:11,543
But four months ago, a rider was added.

510
00:32:11,543 --> 00:32:13,835
If he dies by an accident,
including traffic accidents,

511
00:32:13,835 --> 00:32:16,252
the insurance money doubles.

512
00:32:16,252 --> 00:32:17,335
2.4 billion in total.

513
00:32:17,335 --> 00:32:20,335
Wow, this is insane.

514
00:32:24,919 --> 00:32:29,835
But why would she want the money?

515
00:32:29,835 --> 00:32:32,585
Right. Her father is a judge.

516
00:32:32,585 --> 00:32:34,502
Does she need to kill her husband for money?

517
00:32:34,502 --> 00:32:38,377
She looks wealthy only on the surface.

518
00:32:38,377 --> 00:32:41,543
I asked around, and she is a big spender.

519
00:32:41,543 --> 00:32:44,877
As you can see here.

520
00:32:44,877 --> 00:32:47,710
Golf, travel, what not.

521
00:32:47,710 --> 00:32:51,168
She's constantly juggling credit cards.

522
00:32:51,168 --> 00:32:54,293
Her mother supported her for a while,

523
00:32:54,293 --> 00:32:57,543
until her father found out
and put a stop to it.

524
00:32:57,543 --> 00:33:00,418
The father's not looking good, either.

525
00:33:00,418 --> 00:33:02,460
He invested all his assets in a startup,

526
00:33:02,460 --> 00:33:04,126
which is not doing very well.

527
00:33:04,126 --> 00:33:06,669
He has got nothing except the apartment house.

528
00:33:06,669 --> 00:33:12,252
Han Soo In's husband happens to be
a researcher at the company.

529
00:33:13,126 --> 00:33:16,577
Chimera, Dreaming the Future of Mobility.

530
00:33:19,710 --> 00:33:22,293
Develops simulation platforms,

531
00:33:22,293 --> 00:33:24,452
and researches self-driving techs.

532
00:33:28,043 --> 00:33:30,077
What about the forensic results?

533
00:33:33,835 --> 00:33:35,377
Just as expected.

534
00:33:36,168 --> 00:33:38,460
No brake pressure,

535
00:33:38,460 --> 00:33:40,669
full gas before the accident,

536
00:33:40,669 --> 00:33:42,669
and no mechanical issue.

537
00:33:42,669 --> 00:33:44,669
Driver error, highly likely.

538
00:33:44,669 --> 00:33:46,794
See? I told you it's obvious!

539
00:33:46,794 --> 00:33:49,418
- If that's the case-
- We have two possibilities.

540
00:33:49,418 --> 00:33:52,285
Accidental, or intentional.

541
00:34:00,252 --> 00:34:04,168
[Driver: Han Soo In , Passenger: Baek Sung Min
Victim: Lee Do Hyun]

542
00:34:04,168 --> 00:34:06,710
[Taxi license: Ahn Yong Geon]

543
00:34:06,710 --> 00:34:08,502
[Owner-Driver Taxi]

544
00:34:08,502 --> 00:34:10,293
[Taxi license: Choi Seung Hun]

545
00:34:13,126 --> 00:34:15,002
[Taxi license: Ahn Yong Geon]

546
00:34:19,377 --> 00:34:22,669
I raised So Hee all these years

547
00:34:22,669 --> 00:34:25,252
- with the help of this one.
- Yong Geon.

548
00:34:25,252 --> 00:34:27,002
Hate to part with it, huh?

549
00:34:27,002 --> 00:34:29,627
I would give him mine,

550
00:34:29,627 --> 00:34:32,161
but I still need this job.

551
00:34:32,835 --> 00:34:36,252
But I don't feel so sad

552
00:34:36,252 --> 00:34:38,710
knowing your son will drive it.

553
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:40,335
-Seung Hun?
-Yes?

554
00:34:40,335 --> 00:34:43,502
Take care of her for me.

555
00:34:43,502 --> 00:34:45,585
And make lots of money.

556
00:34:45,585 --> 00:34:49,252
He lowered the price for you.
Be nice to him.

557
00:34:49,252 --> 00:34:51,877
- Think of him as your father.
- No need for that.

558
00:34:51,877 --> 00:34:54,710
I really appreciate it.

559
00:34:54,710 --> 00:34:56,835
Let's meet often.

560
00:34:56,835 --> 00:34:59,161
- Drive safe.
- I will.

561
00:35:01,043 --> 00:35:02,794
Congrats on your new journey.

562
00:35:02,794 --> 00:35:04,043
I will drop by soon.

563
00:35:04,043 --> 00:35:05,502
Let's grab a drink.

564
00:35:05,502 --> 00:35:07,293
Anytime.

565
00:35:07,293 --> 00:35:08,827
Now,

566
00:35:09,710 --> 00:35:11,794
here you go.

567
00:35:11,794 --> 00:35:14,119
-Thank you.
-Sure.

568
00:35:26,377 --> 00:35:28,835
[So Hee's Diner]

569
00:35:36,168 --> 00:35:38,335
What do you mean, autopsy?

570
00:35:38,335 --> 00:35:40,085
- But why?
- We would like to know,

571
00:35:40,085 --> 00:35:43,043
about Mr. Baek's health conditions.

572
00:35:43,043 --> 00:35:46,710
We need to identify the cause
before the cremation.

573
00:35:46,710 --> 00:35:50,460
What are you trying to find out?

574
00:35:50,460 --> 00:35:54,126
What? Is it homicide?

575
00:35:54,126 --> 00:35:56,710
It is still too early too-

576
00:35:56,710 --> 00:35:59,335
I knew something was off.

577
00:35:59,335 --> 00:36:01,877
Why was his airbag the only one disabled?

578
00:36:01,877 --> 00:36:04,002
She is barely injured!

579
00:36:04,002 --> 00:36:05,335
Like I said before,

580
00:36:05,335 --> 00:36:08,285
they shouldn't have got married.

581
00:36:10,210 --> 00:36:11,919
What do you mean?

582
00:36:11,919 --> 00:36:13,585
Why shouldn't they have?

583
00:36:13,585 --> 00:36:15,493
It was an arranged marriage,

584
00:36:16,210 --> 00:36:18,085
from the very beginning.

585
00:36:18,085 --> 00:36:21,669
He arranged the marriage.

586
00:36:21,669 --> 00:36:23,002
That famous judge.

587
00:36:23,002 --> 00:36:24,335
Dr. Baek.

588
00:36:24,335 --> 00:36:26,502
When he was developing

589
00:36:26,502 --> 00:36:28,835
the algorithm or some patent,

590
00:36:28,835 --> 00:36:31,794
the father-in-law offered to invest.

591
00:36:32,543 --> 00:36:35,710
He planned to take my brother
under his wing,

592
00:36:35,710 --> 00:36:38,660
and take my brother's share
of the patent for himself.

593
00:36:41,794 --> 00:36:46,835
If Baek Sung Min is found to have been
killed by accident or sudden acceleration,

594
00:36:46,835 --> 00:36:49,543
his share will go to his next of kin, Han Soo In.

595
00:36:49,543 --> 00:36:52,961
Justice Han will have more control over Chimera.

596
00:36:52,961 --> 00:36:57,418
He gets the share and the money

597
00:36:57,418 --> 00:37:00,502
if no foul play is found.

598
00:37:00,502 --> 00:37:02,293
Hold on.

599
00:37:02,293 --> 00:37:03,919
- Hi, Dad.
- Are you busy?

600
00:37:03,919 --> 00:37:05,877
No, it's okay.

601
00:37:05,877 --> 00:37:08,919
I…

602
00:37:09,710 --> 00:37:11,710
handed over the taxi.

603
00:37:11,710 --> 00:37:14,210
Gang Won and his son came,

604
00:37:14,210 --> 00:37:17,493
and took over the taxi.

605
00:37:18,543 --> 00:37:21,002
You did?

606
00:37:21,002 --> 00:37:22,618
You must be…

607
00:37:23,252 --> 00:37:25,827
- feeling sad.
- Sad?

608
00:37:27,919 --> 00:37:30,126
It's a burden off my shoulders.

609
00:37:30,126 --> 00:37:32,293
Right. I know you worked so hard.

610
00:37:32,293 --> 00:37:33,502
See you at home.

611
00:37:33,502 --> 00:37:35,452
Okay.

612
00:37:38,460 --> 00:37:41,585
Did he sell the taxi?

613
00:37:41,585 --> 00:37:43,627
Yes.

614
00:37:43,627 --> 00:37:46,627
He says he's fine but,

615
00:37:46,627 --> 00:37:48,702
he didn't sound like it.

616
00:37:50,418 --> 00:37:54,126
I wonder what it feels like to quit a job

617
00:37:54,126 --> 00:37:55,835
you worked at for 30 years.

618
00:37:58,002 --> 00:38:00,835
Well, I guess…

619
00:38:03,627 --> 00:38:07,785
he will miss the rumbling
when the engine starts and turns off.

620
00:38:09,543 --> 00:38:13,869
I used to fall asleep hearing that rumbling.

621
00:38:15,210 --> 00:38:19,202
He must feel twice as lost without it.

622
00:38:26,543 --> 00:38:30,085
Chimera does not just make self-driving tech.

623
00:38:30,085 --> 00:38:32,377
It develops thinking machines.

624
00:38:32,377 --> 00:38:35,543
What was Dr. Baek's job here?

625
00:38:35,543 --> 00:38:39,835
He designed ways to assess
threats to people, things, and animals,

626
00:38:39,835 --> 00:38:42,543
and determine which to avoid first.

627
00:38:42,543 --> 00:38:44,752
You mean, which ones to avoid,

628
00:38:44,752 --> 00:38:48,002
and which ones to hit first?

629
00:38:48,002 --> 00:38:51,752
Well, to be more precise,

630
00:38:51,752 --> 00:38:55,293
he designed the logic for the car's assessment.

631
00:38:55,293 --> 00:38:58,952
The algorithm makes the final decision, though.

632
00:39:00,002 --> 00:39:05,418
He always tried to approach it
from humans' perspective.

633
00:39:05,418 --> 00:39:08,043
Beyond simply copying a human,

634
00:39:08,043 --> 00:39:13,002
he wanted the machine to think,
take caution, and evade like humans do.

635
00:39:14,377 --> 00:39:17,293
He focused on avoiding accidents,

636
00:39:17,293 --> 00:39:20,794
and saving humans first.

637
00:39:23,126 --> 00:39:25,085
Losing Dr. Baek's will,

638
00:39:25,085 --> 00:39:27,869
is a big lost to the company.

639
00:39:28,377 --> 00:39:29,994
Yeon Ho?

640
00:39:31,377 --> 00:39:34,502
Palindrome? You are Palindrome, right?

641
00:39:34,502 --> 00:39:36,043
You still remember.

642
00:39:36,043 --> 00:39:37,627
My nickname.

643
00:39:44,043 --> 00:39:47,710
What was it back there? What drome?

644
00:39:47,710 --> 00:39:49,543
Palindrome.

645
00:39:49,543 --> 00:39:52,168
A word that sounds the same
when read backwards.

646
00:39:52,168 --> 00:39:54,285
It's called a palindrome.

647
00:39:55,043 --> 00:39:58,126
Kayak, deed, rotator, noon,
and Yoon-Ji-Yoon.

648
00:39:58,126 --> 00:40:00,335
My name is Yoon Ji Yoon.

649
00:40:00,335 --> 00:40:04,585
Oh, like Woo-Young-Woo! And Lee Hyo-Ii.

650
00:40:04,585 --> 00:40:06,418
- Like that?
- That's right.

651
00:40:06,418 --> 00:40:10,543
Yeon Ho called me that in college.

652
00:40:10,543 --> 00:40:15,119
So you went to the same college?

653
00:40:31,252 --> 00:40:33,418
I still can't believe

654
00:40:33,418 --> 00:40:36,043
what happened to Dr. Baek.

655
00:40:36,043 --> 00:40:37,418
Were you two close?

656
00:40:37,418 --> 00:40:39,877
We did some projects together.

657
00:40:39,877 --> 00:40:42,743
Including the early version of this project.

658
00:40:43,835 --> 00:40:47,961
What was he like at work?

659
00:40:47,961 --> 00:40:50,202
Were there any problems?

660
00:40:53,252 --> 00:40:57,627
There were some conflicts recently.

661
00:40:57,627 --> 00:41:00,043
What do you mean?

662
00:41:00,043 --> 00:41:03,293
They had a big argument during a meeting.

663
00:41:03,293 --> 00:41:05,710
People's lives are at stake!

664
00:41:05,710 --> 00:41:07,835
You can't just wish problems away!

665
00:41:07,835 --> 00:41:11,502
That's gambling, not science!

666
00:41:11,502 --> 00:41:13,035
Sung Min.

667
00:41:14,085 --> 00:41:15,502
I didn't peg you as a coward.

668
00:41:15,502 --> 00:41:16,669
Geun Won…

669
00:41:16,669 --> 00:41:18,919
Mr. Cho and Dr. Baek,

670
00:41:18,919 --> 00:41:21,794
they clashed over AI ethics.

671
00:41:21,794 --> 00:41:24,085
Then Mr. Cho threatened a lawsuit.

672
00:41:24,085 --> 00:41:28,210
He talked about a patent lawsuit,
things like that.

673
00:41:28,210 --> 00:41:33,285
So Dr. Baek was a threat to the company.

674
00:41:34,919 --> 00:41:36,785
Dr. Baek believed that

675
00:41:37,293 --> 00:41:40,335
technology can save humanity.

676
00:41:40,335 --> 00:41:44,710
Above all, he was committed to safety.

677
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:46,752
That's why he took his time,

678
00:41:47,335 --> 00:41:51,994
which may have made
some people uncomfortable.

679
00:42:00,460 --> 00:42:03,252
Look at all the flowers.

680
00:42:03,877 --> 00:42:06,035
I'm starving.

681
00:42:07,710 --> 00:42:09,835
Hey!

682
00:42:09,835 --> 00:42:11,043
The Chief is here!

683
00:42:11,043 --> 00:42:13,335
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

684
00:42:13,335 --> 00:42:15,085
Oh, thank you.

685
00:42:15,085 --> 00:42:17,335
This way.

686
00:42:17,335 --> 00:42:19,418
It's packed with people!

687
00:42:19,418 --> 00:42:20,585
You'll be rich soon.

688
00:42:20,585 --> 00:42:24,002
It's just the opening bloom.

689
00:42:24,002 --> 00:42:26,085
- I'll be right back.
- Do what you need to.

690
00:42:26,085 --> 00:42:27,961
Thank you.

691
00:42:31,919 --> 00:42:34,335
Are they from the Traffic Division?

692
00:42:34,335 --> 00:42:36,502
What are they so excited about?

693
00:42:37,043 --> 00:42:38,418
Huh?

694
00:42:39,085 --> 00:42:42,002
Oh, he's the one!

695
00:42:42,002 --> 00:42:44,543
Ji Dae Se. Or was it Se Dae?

696
00:42:44,543 --> 00:42:47,460
The new pretty boy.

697
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:51,627
Our female officers
were fangirling over him, too.

698
00:42:51,627 --> 00:42:55,085
You call that good looking?
He looks like a girl.

699
00:42:55,085 --> 00:42:58,335
I was a proper heartthrob
when I was his age.

700
00:42:59,752 --> 00:43:01,335
Wow, that's funny.

701
00:43:01,335 --> 00:43:03,002
That was a good one.

702
00:43:03,002 --> 00:43:05,168
It was not a joke.

703
00:43:05,168 --> 00:43:07,710
What are you having? Pork cutlet for me.

704
00:43:07,710 --> 00:43:09,293
Dad!

705
00:43:09,293 --> 00:43:11,377
- You're here!
- Hello.

706
00:43:11,377 --> 00:43:13,919
- Hello.
- My, my.

707
00:43:14,794 --> 00:43:16,002
- Min So Hee!
- Yes?

708
00:43:16,002 --> 00:43:19,168
- Congratulations!
- I… thank you.

709
00:43:19,168 --> 00:43:21,460
It's embarrassing to see my name on the sign.

710
00:43:21,460 --> 00:43:24,377
No, it's heartwarming.

711
00:43:24,377 --> 00:43:26,252
People who heard of you

712
00:43:26,252 --> 00:43:30,877
will definitely want to come here.

713
00:43:30,877 --> 00:43:33,794
- Enjoy your meal.
- You too.

714
00:43:33,794 --> 00:43:36,961
- Enjoy your meal.
- Wait a minute.

715
00:43:36,961 --> 00:43:40,168
What about the former owner?

716
00:43:40,168 --> 00:43:42,585
Her daughter opened a
Korean restaurant in New York.

717
00:43:42,585 --> 00:43:43,752
She is helping her there.

718
00:43:43,752 --> 00:43:44,877
She got a new job.

719
00:43:44,877 --> 00:43:48,293
Why, Korean food is really going global.

720
00:43:48,293 --> 00:43:50,585
K-wave is really a thing.

721
00:43:50,585 --> 00:43:53,252
She was such a nice owner.

722
00:43:53,252 --> 00:43:57,835
She was so lovely, and her food was great.

723
00:43:57,835 --> 00:44:02,035
It was excellent.

724
00:44:02,835 --> 00:44:04,252
Enjoy the food.

725
00:44:04,252 --> 00:44:06,660
- Bon apetit.
- Have a nice meal.

726
00:44:07,627 --> 00:44:09,326
Did you hear?

727
00:44:09,877 --> 00:44:12,460
About the former owner?

728
00:44:12,460 --> 00:44:15,785
Chief tried hitting on her.

729
00:44:16,835 --> 00:44:20,043
What are you doing?

730
00:44:20,043 --> 00:44:21,585
I like you.

731
00:44:21,585 --> 00:44:23,119
What?

732
00:44:23,961 --> 00:44:25,502
Wh-what did you say?

733
00:44:25,502 --> 00:44:27,335
Did you just confess?

734
00:44:27,335 --> 00:44:29,293
Good heavens.

735
00:44:29,293 --> 00:44:30,293
This isn't right.

736
00:44:30,293 --> 00:44:32,085
Oh my goodness.

737
00:44:32,085 --> 00:44:34,835
Why are your eyes so sad?

738
00:44:34,835 --> 00:44:36,543
Confess? Confess what?

739
00:44:36,543 --> 00:44:38,252
Chief got so drunk,

740
00:44:38,252 --> 00:44:41,252
he grabbed her hands and said
she reminds him of his first love.

741
00:44:41,252 --> 00:44:44,502
- Yucks!
- That's just pathetic!

742
00:44:44,502 --> 00:44:46,085
No wonder he got divorced.

743
00:44:46,085 --> 00:44:49,502
Talk about ageing badly.
First love? Give me a break.

744
00:44:49,502 --> 00:44:50,627
Yuck.

745
00:44:50,627 --> 00:44:53,043
Stop being so nosy.

746
00:44:53,043 --> 00:44:54,669
Let's just eat bulgogi.

747
00:44:54,669 --> 00:44:56,126
New owner. It's not bulgogi.

748
00:44:56,126 --> 00:44:58,252
- Right. Jeyuk.
- Jeyuk.

749
00:45:21,252 --> 00:45:23,418
Steering angle log.

750
00:45:23,418 --> 00:45:25,377
[Time / Steering Angle]

751
00:45:25,377 --> 00:45:30,794
2.8 to 12.3 in 0.3 seconds?

752
00:45:36,669 --> 00:45:38,202
Honey!

753
00:45:45,877 --> 00:45:49,002
I hit the brake to the floor,
but it didn't work.

754
00:45:49,002 --> 00:45:51,710
The steering wheel was out of control.

755
00:45:53,585 --> 00:45:56,377
The car went out of control.

756
00:45:56,377 --> 00:45:58,543
The car…

757
00:45:58,543 --> 00:46:01,293
was controlled by someone?

758
00:46:02,919 --> 00:46:04,585
I knew it.

759
00:46:05,126 --> 00:46:07,210
- Have you eaten?
- No.

760
00:46:07,210 --> 00:46:11,043
Don't skip your meal.
Otherwise, what's the point?

761
00:46:11,043 --> 00:46:13,085
My father's side dishes and kimchi.

762
00:46:13,085 --> 00:46:15,710
- Mix them up and-
- Let's go.

763
00:46:15,710 --> 00:46:18,627
Go where? You need to eat.

764
00:46:18,627 --> 00:46:20,460
Come and find out.

765
00:46:20,460 --> 00:46:22,126
Eat first, then go.

766
00:46:23,002 --> 00:46:24,535
Let's go now.

767
00:46:34,502 --> 00:46:36,919
Sorry, I know it's late.

768
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:38,585
Save it for later.

769
00:46:47,418 --> 00:46:50,543
[TCU: Transmission Control Unit]
These are TCU and ADAS ESCU logs, right?

770
00:46:50,543 --> 00:46:53,502
[ADAS ECU: Advanced Driver Assistance Systems]
They match the case records.

771
00:46:53,502 --> 00:46:57,418
That's weird.
These are not typical driving patterns.

772
00:46:57,418 --> 00:47:01,043
A conditional execution routine is hidden here.

773
00:47:03,293 --> 00:47:05,243
Someone wrote it in.

774
00:47:06,835 --> 00:47:08,418
What do you mean?

775
00:47:08,418 --> 00:47:10,502
You mean the car didn't malfunction?

776
00:47:10,502 --> 00:47:12,293
Someone planned it?

777
00:47:12,293 --> 00:47:16,252
Here. The condition includes a GPS coordinate.

778
00:47:16,252 --> 00:47:19,293
Road ID: D894X.

779
00:47:19,293 --> 00:47:21,043
Where is it?

780
00:47:21,043 --> 00:47:22,618
Hold on a sec.

781
00:47:23,126 --> 00:47:26,043
Naeguro 20-gil, Bunjeong-gu,
Seonghan-si, Gyeonggi-do.

782
00:47:26,043 --> 00:47:27,460
That's where the car crashed.

783
00:47:27,460 --> 00:47:29,460
Was it the trigger?

784
00:47:29,460 --> 00:47:31,669
One more thing.

785
00:47:31,669 --> 00:47:34,335
Here, "passenger seat occupied."

786
00:47:34,335 --> 00:47:37,043
There must be a passenger.

787
00:47:37,043 --> 00:47:38,835
If the two conditions are met,

788
00:47:38,835 --> 00:47:40,919
the hidden command is executed.

789
00:47:40,919 --> 00:47:43,460
The car accelerates,

790
00:47:43,460 --> 00:47:45,460
steering fixed at 12.3 degrees,

791
00:47:45,460 --> 00:47:48,418
and the brake don't work.

792
00:47:48,418 --> 00:47:52,919
What do you mean?
When the car reaches this road,

793
00:47:52,919 --> 00:47:54,752
it starts to move on its own?

794
00:47:54,752 --> 00:47:57,168
Dr. Baek was the target.

795
00:47:57,168 --> 00:47:59,710
He was a dead man

796
00:47:59,710 --> 00:48:01,994
the moment he got in the car.

797
00:48:03,669 --> 00:48:07,335
It was not an accident.
It was a murder by design.

798
00:48:09,627 --> 00:48:13,669
Someone hacked a car to kill?

799
00:48:13,669 --> 00:48:15,794
Who would do such a…

800
00:48:16,669 --> 00:48:18,285
Mr. Cho.

801
00:48:18,794 --> 00:48:20,126
As long-time partners,

802
00:48:20,126 --> 00:48:22,961
he and Dr. Baek developed the system together.

803
00:48:30,085 --> 00:48:31,418
A murder?

804
00:48:31,418 --> 00:48:35,543
A murder disguised as
driver error or malfunction.

805
00:48:36,210 --> 00:48:37,835
Come to think of it, when I went to NFS,

806
00:48:37,835 --> 00:48:40,085
Researcher Kang told me something.

807
00:48:40,085 --> 00:48:43,543
Some data were missing
right before the collision.

808
00:48:43,543 --> 00:48:45,835
[CAN: Controller Area Network]
CAN data.

809
00:48:45,835 --> 00:48:49,293
- Yeah, that.
- CAN data? What's that?

810
00:48:49,293 --> 00:48:52,585
In the car's internal network,

811
00:48:52,585 --> 00:48:55,252
some data were removed
or not recorded on purpose.

812
00:48:55,252 --> 00:48:59,335
The missing section must be
when the command was executed.

813
00:48:59,335 --> 00:49:02,252
The culprit is working for Chimera, then!

814
00:49:06,168 --> 00:49:09,210
How long have you been there?

815
00:49:09,210 --> 00:49:12,293
- Since a while ago.
- I called him.

816
00:49:12,293 --> 00:49:14,961
Superintendent wants us to take him in.

817
00:49:14,961 --> 00:49:18,002
Why? What are we, babysitters?

818
00:49:18,002 --> 00:49:19,794
Who knows?

819
00:49:19,794 --> 00:49:21,460
Like they say,
a good smith can shape any iron.

820
00:49:21,460 --> 00:49:24,002
With polishing, he might
become our greatest asset.

821
00:49:24,002 --> 00:49:26,710
I'll make a great blacksmith, sir!

822
00:49:26,710 --> 00:49:28,085
That's not what I meant.

823
00:49:28,085 --> 00:49:32,002
Okay. I can't promise you anything,
but come here and observe.

824
00:49:32,002 --> 00:49:33,585
Thank you, ma'am!

825
00:49:35,919 --> 00:49:37,961
Raise your hand first
before you say something.

826
00:49:37,961 --> 00:49:40,002
- Okay?
- Yes, sir!

827
00:49:40,002 --> 00:49:41,835
Just like that.

828
00:49:41,835 --> 00:49:44,377
Such a crime can be committed

829
00:49:44,377 --> 00:49:46,627
only by someone working for Chimera.

830
00:49:46,627 --> 00:49:49,002
That's right, considering the MO.

831
00:49:49,002 --> 00:49:52,418
Someone related to that company.
where Baek Sung Min used to work?

832
00:49:52,418 --> 00:49:57,335
You're on the right track.
So, our focus is on this guy.

833
00:49:57,335 --> 00:49:59,919
Cho Geun Won, CEO of Chimera.

834
00:49:59,919 --> 00:50:03,335
He frequently clashed with Baek Sung Min
over the company's IPO.

835
00:50:03,335 --> 00:50:07,502
He's one of the few people
with the knowledge to do this.

836
00:50:07,502 --> 00:50:09,752
Cho Geun Won. Double check.

837
00:50:18,085 --> 00:50:20,335
Can I help you?

838
00:50:20,335 --> 00:50:23,577
- My name is Cho Geun Won.
- Nice to meet you.

839
00:50:24,335 --> 00:50:26,285
Cho Geun Won?

840
00:50:27,210 --> 00:50:29,126
- Cho Geun Won!
- Yes, Mr. Cho!

841
00:50:29,126 --> 00:50:30,752
May I ask what you're doing here?

842
00:50:30,752 --> 00:50:32,835
Hi. Sorry for the interruption.

843
00:50:32,835 --> 00:50:35,168
I have something to give you.

844
00:50:35,168 --> 00:50:36,835
Oh.

845
00:50:36,835 --> 00:50:40,669
- We're having a meeting. This way.
- Apologies.

846
00:50:40,669 --> 00:50:42,410
Take care.

847
00:50:44,585 --> 00:50:46,126
This way.

848
00:50:51,168 --> 00:50:52,543
Wow.

849
00:50:57,502 --> 00:51:01,669
Something came up during a security check.

850
00:51:02,877 --> 00:51:03,919
What…

851
00:51:03,919 --> 00:51:09,919
Someone accessed Ms. Han's car
from one of our computers.

852
00:51:09,919 --> 00:51:14,710
It was not a simple diagnosis.
I found an auto execution protocol.

853
00:51:14,710 --> 00:51:19,285
It can fix the car's speed, disable
the brake, and control steering.

854
00:51:20,502 --> 00:51:26,585
I think someone staged the accident,

855
00:51:26,585 --> 00:51:28,585
to take Dr. Baek's life.

856
00:51:29,168 --> 00:51:32,293
Do you know who accessed it?

857
00:51:34,877 --> 00:51:36,994
I checked the account.

858
00:51:37,877 --> 00:51:40,493
It belonged to Yoon Ji Yoon.

859
00:51:41,418 --> 00:51:44,919
Unfortunately, security camera
clips have been erased.

860
00:51:44,919 --> 00:51:47,210
- Erased?
- Yes.

861
00:51:47,210 --> 00:51:48,919
I found the access log,

862
00:51:48,919 --> 00:51:52,002
but camera recordings
around that time are gone.

863
00:51:52,002 --> 00:51:55,660
So, I copied all available files.

864
00:51:59,335 --> 00:52:02,752
We'll take a look at it.

865
00:52:02,752 --> 00:52:05,835
I'm not sure it's appropriate,

866
00:52:05,835 --> 00:52:07,794
but there were rumors

867
00:52:07,794 --> 00:52:12,585
that Yoon Ji Yoon and Dr. Baek,

868
00:52:12,585 --> 00:52:14,168
were lovers.

869
00:52:14,710 --> 00:52:17,710
But they seem to have fell out recently.

870
00:52:17,710 --> 00:52:20,210
More recently, Dr. Baek

871
00:52:20,210 --> 00:52:23,161
removed Yoon Ji Yoon from his project.

872
00:52:30,377 --> 00:52:32,210
Log files,

873
00:52:33,293 --> 00:52:35,660
access time,

874
00:52:39,085 --> 00:52:42,168
command structure.
There are no signs of tampering.

875
00:52:42,168 --> 00:52:45,252
It was her account, then?

876
00:52:45,252 --> 00:52:46,961
Technically, yes.

877
00:52:46,961 --> 00:52:50,418
She has a motive, if what Mr. Cho said is true.

878
00:52:50,418 --> 00:52:54,210
If she was kicked from the project
and her relationship went sour,

879
00:52:54,210 --> 00:52:57,418
she lost both her position and lover.

880
00:52:57,418 --> 00:53:00,252
Does that make sense? Her, of all people?

881
00:53:00,252 --> 00:53:02,919
-Who's Yoon Ji Yoon, anyway?
-Do we know her?

882
00:53:02,919 --> 00:53:06,252
Inspector Cha's college friend. Palindrome.

883
00:53:06,252 --> 00:53:07,543
What drome?

884
00:53:07,543 --> 00:53:09,043
It can be someone else.

885
00:53:09,043 --> 00:53:12,335
Employees have easy access
to their coworkers' terminals.

886
00:53:12,335 --> 00:53:16,168
That's possible.
However, Ji Yoon had an admin account.

887
00:53:16,168 --> 00:53:18,252
To access the account,
the user needs to know the ID,

888
00:53:18,252 --> 00:53:21,961
access a set computer,
and pass the authenticator.

889
00:53:21,961 --> 00:53:23,919
Okay, I get the situation.

890
00:53:23,919 --> 00:53:27,452
But do you also think
that Yoon Ji Yoon is responsible?

891
00:53:28,460 --> 00:53:31,869
We have to find out.

892
00:53:45,585 --> 00:53:47,877
[SIM log / IPO data. Driving test results]

893
00:54:12,627 --> 00:54:15,210
Yeon Ho? What are you doing here?

894
00:54:15,210 --> 00:54:16,710
We need to talk.

895
00:54:16,710 --> 00:54:18,293
Me too.

896
00:54:19,043 --> 00:54:21,335
Get in. We'll talk in the car.

897
00:54:21,335 --> 00:54:23,002
Okay.

898
00:54:23,002 --> 00:54:25,460
You seem to be in a hurry.

899
00:54:26,252 --> 00:54:29,669
- What did you want to talk about?
- You go first.

900
00:54:29,669 --> 00:54:31,168
You first.

901
00:54:32,502 --> 00:54:35,126
What is your relationship with Dr. Baek?

902
00:54:35,126 --> 00:54:37,460
They say you had an affair with him,

903
00:54:37,460 --> 00:54:40,585
but you were removed from the project,

904
00:54:40,585 --> 00:54:43,085
along with your access to key codes.

905
00:54:43,085 --> 00:54:44,210
That's-

906
00:54:44,210 --> 00:54:46,252
Is that why you did it?

907
00:54:46,252 --> 00:54:48,168
Because he betrayed you?

908
00:54:48,168 --> 00:54:50,377
Or did you kill him

909
00:54:50,377 --> 00:54:52,410
so you can take his place?

910
00:54:56,335 --> 00:54:59,585
Oh my. I'm sorry.

911
00:54:59,585 --> 00:55:02,669
I don't know what got into me.

912
00:55:02,669 --> 00:55:04,243
You better drive.

913
00:55:17,418 --> 00:55:21,043
Dr. Baek couldn't deal
with the fact that his project

914
00:55:21,043 --> 00:55:25,168
became a chessboard for capital and power play.

915
00:55:25,168 --> 00:55:27,418
Mr. Cho and Justice Han
gave him so much pressure,

916
00:55:27,418 --> 00:55:31,752
and threatened to kick Dr. Baek
from his own project.

917
00:55:31,752 --> 00:55:33,002
In that case,

918
00:55:33,002 --> 00:55:35,877
someone had to see the project
through to the end.

919
00:55:35,877 --> 00:55:39,460
That's why he removed me from the project,

920
00:55:39,460 --> 00:55:42,585
to take all the responsibilities.

921
00:55:42,585 --> 00:55:45,543
We found records of someone
hacking into Ms. Han's car.

922
00:55:45,543 --> 00:55:49,460
Your account ran the protocol.
I need explanation.

923
00:55:49,460 --> 00:55:53,377
Cho Geun Won did it. I just found out today.

924
00:55:53,377 --> 00:55:58,035
I also found out what he did
to get the IPO going.

925
00:56:02,126 --> 00:56:04,210
To get better performance,

926
00:56:04,210 --> 00:56:08,168
Mr. Cho was using a risky logic
in real world driving tests.

927
00:56:08,168 --> 00:56:12,460
It ignores sensors and fixes response times

928
00:56:12,460 --> 00:56:16,827
to make it look like self-driving is working.

929
00:56:17,585 --> 00:56:20,043
Can you prove that?

930
00:56:20,043 --> 00:56:22,077
The evidence is in that bag.

931
00:56:35,252 --> 00:56:38,126
- What is it?
- The brake feels off.

932
00:56:38,126 --> 00:56:39,335
Are you pressing the gas?

933
00:56:39,335 --> 00:56:41,961
No, but the car is…

934
00:56:41,961 --> 00:56:43,543
The brake!

935
00:56:43,543 --> 00:56:45,502
The brake is acting weird!

936
00:56:51,377 --> 00:56:54,085
Hit a wall! Slow the car down!

937
00:57:30,627 --> 00:57:32,252
Cell runaway imminent evacuate now.

938
00:57:32,252 --> 00:57:33,752
Get out.

939
00:57:34,543 --> 00:57:36,543
The door won't open!

940
00:57:42,961 --> 00:57:44,877
Come on, come on!

941
00:57:44,877 --> 00:57:46,752
The bag!

942
00:57:48,710 --> 00:57:50,460
Hurry!

943
00:58:58,752 --> 00:59:00,919
The only one capable
of committing this crime is…

944
00:59:00,919 --> 00:59:02,502
Baek Sung Min is already dead.

945
00:59:02,502 --> 00:59:03,794
He's the victim.

946
00:59:03,794 --> 00:59:06,126
Are you saying Han Soo In
could have murdered him?

947
00:59:06,126 --> 00:59:08,043
Let's find out.

948
00:59:08,043 --> 00:59:09,669
It's not over.

949
00:59:15,585 --> 00:59:17,377
Why did you suddenly take your clothes off?

950
00:59:17,377 --> 00:59:19,752
Train as if it's real.

951
00:59:19,752 --> 00:59:21,418
I have to be somewhere.

952
00:59:21,418 --> 00:59:23,543
The brake isn't working.
